{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And these you shall detest among the birds.</b> That is, from among the clean birds, and this teaches you that the clean birds are more numerous than the unclean; and so our Rabbis of blessed memory stated. Therefore the verse specified the unclean ones for you. Hence they said: a person should always teach his student the short way — like a person who says to his fellow, 'clarify this from within that,' for reason dictates that the species he is selecting from within it is the more numerous of what is being sifted. And upon this the verse says (Leviticus 20:25): ״והבדלתם בין הבהמה הטהורה לטמאה ובין העוף הטמא לטהור״ — it placed the clean beast before the unclean, but for the bird it placed the unclean before the clean; that is, you shall clarify the clean beast from among the unclean, and this indicates that the unclean beasts are more numerous than the clean; and you shall clarify the unclean bird from among the clean, and this indicates that the clean birds are more numerous than the unclean. Therefore the verse specified the unclean ones for you, to teach you the short way." "<b>And Ramban</b> of blessed memory wrote that the sign of the unclean birds is the דריסה (seizing with the talons): every bird that seizes is always unclean, as our Rabbis of blessed memory mentioned, for the Torah distanced it because its blood is heated toward cruelty, and is black and coarse, and it produces burned black bile and instills cruelty in the heart. And the meaning of דריסה is hunting prey — that it pursues and seizes them alive and tramples them in its grip and eats them, as the coarse hawk called אסטו״ר and the hawk called אשפרוי״ר do. And the reason for the prohibition of the birds is because of the cruelty of their natures. And the beasts too, it is possible that the reason is the same, for among those that chew the cud and split the hoof and are cloven, none are birds of prey, whereas all the others are predators." "<b>And behold,</b> it is found in their natural history a difference from what the Sages mentioned, that all the fat of clean animals congeals, while the fat of all unclean animals never coagulates and never hardens — and behold, they are different. And from this it is possible that they cause harm to the organs of generation, and the seed that is gathered from the moisture within them would be cold and wet, bearing no offspring at all, or not bearing well and properly — apart from the fact that in the permitted ones there is a known benefit in the way of medicine." "<b>And I saw</b> in certain books of medicine that the fat of a pig, if a nursing infant suckles from it, that lad will become a leper — and this is a sign that in all of them there are very evil natural properties, end quote. <br><b>And furthermore,</b> one may give another reason for the prohibition of the birds: since the Holy One, blessed be He, chooses the good and loves lowliness and all other good traits, and hates cruelty and all other evil traits, therefore He chose for His offerings the creatures that are lowly and gentle, and from those that He, may He be exalted, chose for the offering, He commanded Israel that their food should be from them. And just as He, blessed be He, distances the unclean birds for the purpose of the offering, so too He distances them for the purpose of Israel's food — and all this to teach us that He, may He be exalted, hates the trait of evil and cruelty, and loves the trait of goodness and lowliness and gentleness. And for this reason the prophets compare the wicked and those of cruel nature to unclean birds of prey, as it is written (Jeremiah 49): ״הנה כנשר יעלה וידאה ויפרוש כנפיו על בצרה״, and it is written (Deuteronomy 28): ״ישא ה׳ עליך גוי מרחוק מקצה הארץ כאשר ידאה הנשר״, and likewise they further compare them to beasts and wild animals of prey, as it is written (Jeremiah 5): ״על כן הכם אריה ביער זאב ערבות ישדדם נמר שוקד על עריהם״, and King David, of blessed memory, mentioned (Psalms 58): ״מלתעות כפירים נתוץ ה׳״, (ibid. 57): ״נפשי בתוך לבאים אשכבה״. And they compare the righteous, possessors of good traits, lovers of peace and integrity, to gentle beasts and pure birds, as it is written (Isaiah 5): ״ורעו כבשים כדברם״, and it is written (Malachi 3): ״ויצאתם ופשתם כעגלי מרבק״, and it is written (Hosea 11): ״יחרדו כצפור ממצרים וכיונה מארץ אשור״, and it is written (Isaiah 60): ״וכיונים אל ארובותיהם״." "<b>And furthermore,</b> one may say another reason for the prohibition of the birds: because divination is practiced only with unclean birds, and the Torah stated (Leviticus 19): ״לא תנחשו״. Therefore it forbade all the unclean birds both on account of divination and on account of the fact that they are birds of prey — for every bird that has prowess in דריסה (seizing) has prowess in divination, and it is fit to rely upon it more, and so the masters of divination say. And the divination of the unclean bird is that it changes its behavior and changes its resting place from place to place, and sometimes it plucks its wings — and everyone knows and recognizes that it is revealing something, except that not everyone understands it, only the wise diviner. And the divination of the clean bird is not called divination, because what it reveals to human beings is only through the sound of its call and chirping — and this, even among unclean birds, is not called divination but wisdom, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said: the speech of date palms, the speech of birds, and the speech of trees. And upon this Solomon said in his wisdom (Ecclesiastes 10): ״עוף השמים יוליך את הקול״ — that this is not divination of deed but divination of speech, and it is not called divination but wisdom, of the species of wisdoms — and it resembles what the verse says (Isaiah 30): ״ואזניך תשמענה דבר מאחריך לאמר זה הדרך לכו בו״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {3 "Citations are given as the author wrote them; Jeremiah references are Jeremiah 49:22, Jeremiah 5:6. Psalms 58:7, 57:5. Isaiah 5:17, 60:8.", 4 "Leviticus citation is Leviticus 19:26; Ecclesiastes 10:20; Isaiah 30:21."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:05.948639645Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}